2	// Saved-card / off-session charging primitives for subscription renewals.
3	//
4	// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
5	// Until now a renewal could only debit the wallet (`worker/billing.ts` ->
6	// `debitWallet`). A customer with a perfectly good card on file was suspended the
7	// moment their wallet emptied, because `User.stripePaymentMethodId` was never
8	// written and never read. Everything needed to charge a card lives here; the
9	// worker owns the *policy* (when to retry, when to suspend), this module owns the
10	// *mechanics* (attach a card, charge it, credit the wallet for what it paid).
11	//
12	// THE MONEY MODEL — identical to checkout, deliberately
13	// Checkout applies wallet credit first and puts only the remainder on the card
14	// (`lib/wallet-split.ts`). Renewals now do the same: the card is charged the
15	// remainder, that exact amount is CREDITED to the wallet, and the existing
16	// CAS-guarded renewal transaction debits the FULL renewal from the wallet. So the
17	// wallet is always the thing that pays the bill and the card is always just a way
18	// to fund the wallet — one money path, already proven, and a partial failure can
19	// never half-apply a renewal.
20	//
21	// Plain server module (NOT "use server"): imported by the worker, by server
22	// actions and by server components. `lib/stripe.ts` is not modified by this file.
23	
24	import type Stripe from "stripe";
